  "finalText": "I built the \"Revenue by quarter\" bar chart: a 6 s, 1920×1080 composition on a light background, with the title top-left.\n\n- **Axis:** **Baseline axis** draws on from left to right first (0.3–0.9 s).\n- **Bars:** **Bar Q1–Q4** grow up from the baseline one after another, starting at 1.0, 1.2, 1.4 and 1.6 s, with an Expo Out ease.\n- **Values:** **Value $12M–$27M** fade in and rise slightly above each bar, starting about 0.4 s into each bar's growth.\n- **Q4 highlight:** **Bar Q4** and its label use orange (#F97316 bar, #C2410C text). After it lands, it gets a small pop (to 104% wide, 102% tall) that settles by 2.9 s.\n- **Labels:** **Quarter labels** Q1–Q4 sit under the baseline and fade in at 0.9 s.\n\nI checked the frames at 0.5, 1.2, 1.9, 2.5 and 3.5 s and the sequence reads correctly; the chart holds from about 2.9 s to the end.\n\nOne deviation: the value labels fade and rise in rather than counting up. Animating the number itself needs an expression, which I didn't add. I can add a count-up if you want it."
